Build the USB HID gamepad (hw/usb/dev-gamepad.c, overlaid from
gamepad/qemu/ by scripts/prepare-qemu.sh). M13 path A,
docs/tracks/m13-gamepads.md.

QEMU has no gamepad of any kind — hw/input/hid.h knows HID_MOUSE,
HID_TABLET and HID_KEYBOARD and nothing else, and the input core has no
axis event a joystick could ride — so this is a whole device rather than
a switch to turn on. It is its own file, not a fourth kind in dev-hid.c,
because every machine this project makes already has a usb-tablet on that
code and a gamepad has no business perturbing it.

Wired under CONFIG_USB_HID rather than a symbol of its own: that config
is `bool / default y / depends on USB` (hw/usb/Kconfig), so it is exactly
"this machine has USB", which is the only condition a gamepad has. A
machine built without USB gets neither.

The host side drives it through usb_gamepad_set_state()
(gamepad/qemu/usb-gamepad.h), called from the embed shim's input bottom
half under the BQL — absolute state rather than events, so a dropped
update is corrected by the next one instead of leaving a button held.

diff --git a/hw/usb/meson.build b/hw/usb/meson.build
index ba55c28ef6..284acd7dda 100644
--- a/hw/usb/meson.build
+++ b/hw/usb/meson.build
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_XLNX_USB_SUBSYS', if_true: files('xlnx-usb-subsystem
 # emulated usb devices
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_USB_HUB', if_true: files('dev-hub.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_USB_HID', if_true: files('dev-hid.c'))
+system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_USB_HID', if_true: files('dev-gamepad.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_USB_TABLET_WACOM', if_true: files('dev-wacom.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_USB_STORAGE_CORE', if_true: files('dev-storage.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_USB_STORAGE_BOT', if_true: files('dev-storage-bot.c'))
